# PromoteObstacle — convert a transient observation or a pending proposal
# into a user-validated permanent keepout polygon.
#
# After the obstacle-tracker decouple (2026-05-07), map_server no longer
# auto-mirrors /obstacle_tracker/obstacles into the classification layer
# or obstacle_polygons_. The tracker output is for monitoring only. To
# turn one of those tracker observations (or any user-drawn polygon)
# into a permanent keepout, the GUI calls this service.
#
# Since 2026-08-24 the wheel-slip dig detector follows the same rule: a
# dig no longer writes itself into areas.dat. map_server stamps a
# PENDING keepout at the spot — live in the mask for this session so
# coverage cannot re-dig the same hole, but never persisted — and the
# operator accepts it here (pending_id) or discards it with
# ~/discard_obstacle.
#
# Effects:
#   * The polygon is appended to the target area's obstacles list (or, on
#     the pending path, the existing proposal is marked accepted).
#   * Cells inside become NO_GO_ZONE in the classification layer.
#   * The keepout mask is rebuilt so Smac/Nav2 see the polygon as lethal.
#   * The area YAML is persisted so the obstacle survives restart.
#   * Reachability BFS is re-run for the area (DEAD recompute).
#
# Exactly one of the three lookup paths is used, in this order:
#   * pending_id != 0   → accept the PENDING obstacle carrying this
#                          MapObstacleInfo.id (any area — area_index is
#                          ignored). The polygon is already live; this
#                          only clears the pending flag and persists it.
#                          Note: re-sending the same polygon instead
#                          would hit the centroid dedup guard and be a
#                          silent no-op, which is why this path exists.
#   * polygon set       → use the polygon directly. Free-form path for
#                          user-drawn keepouts.
#   * obstacle_id != 0  → look up the tracked obstacle with this id in
#                          the most recent /obstacle_tracker/obstacles
#                          snapshot (cached in map_server) and use its
#                          polygon. Easiest GUI path: "promote tracker #N".

# Target area (must be a mowing area, not a navigation area).
# Ignored on the pending_id path — the proposal already knows its area.
uint32 area_index

# Either look up the tracker observation by id (recommended), or supply
# a polygon directly. If both are set, polygon wins.
uint32 obstacle_id
geometry_msgs/Polygon polygon

# Accept the pending proposal with this MapObstacleInfo.id (0 = unused).
# Takes precedence over polygon and obstacle_id.
uint32 pending_id

# Operator-facing label stored with the keepout ("apple tree"). Empty
# keeps the existing name on the pending path, and leaves a tracker- or
# user-supplied polygon unnamed.
string name
---
bool success
string message
